### 4. How to Run & Test

1. **Install dependencies**:
   ```powershell
   npm install express mongoose
   ```
2. **Start the database**: Ensure MongoDB is running locally on port `27017`.
3. **Start the server**:
   ```powershell
   node MyServer.js
   ```
4. **Test the endpoints**: You can use Postman, curl, or any REST client using the JSON request samples documented in [`ReadME-Epress-MongoDB`](file:///d:/web%20dev/Training/MERN-training/UI-development/16-ExpressJS-NodeJS-DB-ReactJS/I1-ExpressJS-Http-MongoDB-CRUD/ReadME-Epress-MongoDB).